+By B.24a the scheme-theoretic image of $\pi_A$ is the finite constant
+subgroup cut out, on each minimal component, by $X^2-X=Y_1^2-Y_1=0$.
+The point $\rho$ lies in this image, whereas $u(\rho)$ does not:
+$\epsilon^2-\epsilon=\epsilon\ne0$.  A compatible automorphism
+would have to preserve this image, a contradiction.  Faithful flatness
+does not annihilate this nonzero element.  The full integral cocycle and
+the exact dual-number test are verified in
+\texttt{g\_signed\_fermat2.py}.  This is an incompatibility obstruction,
+stronger than a failure of reconstruction from generator images.
+\end{proof}
